{title: Michael, Row the Boat Ashore}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}
{meta: public_domain African-American spiritual from the Sea Islands of South Carolina, published in 1867 in "Slave Songs of the United States". Only the refrain and verses from that collection are used.}
{meta: source Allen, Ware and Garrison, Slave Songs of the United States, 1867 (spelling modernised).}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Michael, row the boat a[Em]shore, [F]Halle[C]lujah!
[C]Michael, row the [Em]boat a[Dm]shore, [C]Halle[G]lu[C]jah!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[C]Sister, help to trim the [Em]boat, [F]Halle[C]lujah!
[C]Sister, help to [Em]trim the [Dm]boat, [C]Halle[G]lu[C]jah!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
